WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.180
From "Young Leonard" to a show about&nbsp;
Penny's journey as a new mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.760
fans of The Big Bang Theory&nbsp;
have all kinds of ideas about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.400
what the upcoming spin-off should be&nbsp;
about. Here's what they're saying.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.660
The Big Bang Theory is returning to television...&nbsp;
kind of. According to The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.540
during a press event for tons of&nbsp;
different Warner Bros. properties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.460
it was announced that Max — the streamer formerly&nbsp;
known as HBO Max — will be home to a brand new Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.900
Bang Theory spin-off. Chuck Lorre, who created&nbsp;
the original for CBS alongside Bill Prady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.380
will also be involved. Max has been the&nbsp;
exclusive streaming home of The Big Bang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.800
Theory for a while now, so this doesn't&nbsp;
come as a shock. Whether or not there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.400
more ground to cover in the Big Bang Theory&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe is a question, though.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.960
"Oh good, they used my NASA picture."

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.680
Whatever this show will cover is up in the&nbsp;
air, and Lorre and his team are remaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.360
tight-lipped — but back in 2019, he did tell&nbsp;
The Hollywood Reporter he was open to spin-offs:

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.260
"Truthfully, the reason for a spinoff is&nbsp;
economics, and that's not the reason to do a show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.980
You should do a show because you have something&nbsp;
you really love and you want to do it. Economics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.420
follow passion. If you start with economics&nbsp;
... well, s--t, become a network executive."

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.900
Obviously, there's already one Big Bang&nbsp;
spin-off, which is the apparent result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.980
of Chuck Lorre walking into the main CBS&nbsp;
office and simply pitching "what if Sheldon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.000
but young?" Since 2017, Young Sheldon&nbsp;
has been an enormous hit for the network,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.640
and now, Max will have their own&nbsp;
potential Lorre hit on their hands.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.580
There's any range of things this&nbsp;
spin-off could focus on — perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.400
a younger version of a different&nbsp;
character, like Howard Wolowitz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.180
in college? Lorre did rule out a spin-off&nbsp;
of Leonard and Penny Hofstadter's journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.420
into parenthood after Penny discovered&nbsp;
she was pregnant in the series finale.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.610
"My head is wrapped."

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:29.501
"Well, if something else was wrapped&nbsp;
we wouldn't be in this situation."

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.160
Back in 2019, Lorre told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.940
"No. [...] I feel like these seven characters&nbsp;
share seven different areas of the same brain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.140
We have split them off in every single different&nbsp;
division you can and it all works. There's no two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.560
that don't work together. I don't think it would&nbsp;
be a disaster, but it wouldn't be Big Bang."

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.880
Considering how out-of-the-blue news of yet&nbsp;
another Big Bang Theory show was, it only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.080
makes sense that it has elicited strong reactions.&nbsp;
Folks have rushed to social media to share their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.690
feelings on the impending spin-off and suffice&nbsp;
to say, the online masses have mixed feelings.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:57.940
One person wrote on Twitter:

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.580
"I love this show, but like [...] Why?"

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.480
"And it's done." " Yup we're all in." "Alright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.050
I'll see you guys in 20 years."

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.760
And this person isn't the only one asking that&nbsp;
question. Numerous people are questioning why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.360
there needs to be another entry in the Big&nbsp;
Bang Theory franchise. Another fan wrote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.080
on Twitter that they are more than happy with&nbsp;
leaving the franchise behind once Young Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.580
concludes. Meanwhile, one Twitter user, among many&nbsp;
others, can't hide their disappointment over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.840
seemingly endless stream of sequels, prequels, and&nbsp;
reboots that plague modern Hollywood as a whole.

00:02:28.935 --> 00:02:29.523
"I knew it!"

00:02:29.523 --> 00:02:33.180
At the same time, there are quite a few people&nbsp;
who've voiced their support for the new show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.720
For example, a Big Bang fan wrote on Twitter&nbsp;
that they're hopeful that the series could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.680
follow Penny's younger years with Katey Sagal&nbsp;
back as her mother. Another Twitter user came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.280
up with a pitch of their own for a program&nbsp;
dedicated to Penny's goofy ex, Zack Johnson.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.520
"How can you bounce stuff off&nbsp;
the moon if there's no gravity?"

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.580
Meanwhile, another person wrote on&nbsp;
the social media site that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.700
Big Bang spin-off is coming together&nbsp;
in response to the success of Young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.240
Sheldon — so they tossed out the idea of&nbsp;
having it focus on Leonard's childhood.

